      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sherwood Park began as Campbelltown in 1953, but Canada Post renamed it Sherwood Park in 1956 to avoid confusion with other towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherwood_Park",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sherwood Park’s Heritage Mile preserves old landmarks like the Ottewell homestead, offering a living window into the county’s pioneer past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherwood_Park",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ukrainian Cultural Heritage Village in Sherwood Park brings pioneer life to life with costumed interpreters reenacting early settlers’ daily routines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://sherwoodparkchamber.com/tourism-strathcona-county-sherwood-park/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sherwood Park sits within Alberta’s Industrial Heartland, hosting Canada’s largest hydrocarbon refining cluster.",
